Author: Wallace Chan <naahtec@hotmail.com>
Date:   Wed Jun 10 22:50:57 2026 -0400

    skill: #11144 Iter 40 — G10 close: alias is sole truth for statusline label
    
    Operator: keep literals + drop statusline.sh hardcoded fallback.
    
    `statusline.sh:165-177` had a tiered fallback for the role label:
      1. config-resolved alias (used if different from $ROLE)
      2. hardcoded `PM`/`QA`/`DM` uppercase fallback (used when $ROLE
         already matched the alias and matched one of the 3 known names)
      3. raw $ROLE otherwise
    
    The hardcoded uppercase tier caused doc/script coupling: L2 docs
    (dm/pm/verifier/instructions.md) carried literal `` `PM`/`QA`/`DM` ``
    labels matching the uppercase fallback's output. The literals were
    correct on installs where the alias == role-class name AND the script's
    tier-2 fired (e.g. PM agent ALIAS=pm, ROLE=pm → "PM"), but broke on
    installs where verifier was aliased something other than `qa` — the
    verifier doc would still say `` `QA` role label `` while the statusline
    would show the actual alias.
    
    Closes by making alias the sole truth:
    
    1. statusline.sh: dropped the PM/QA/DM uppercase tier. ROLE_LABEL now
       == ALIAS (when alias resolves to something different from $ROLE) or
       raw $ROLE (when alias == $ROLE or no alias config).
    
    2. L2 docs: replaced the 4 literal labels with `[ROLE]` placeholder
       substitution, so the composed CLAUDE.md renders the actual install
       alias per role.
    
    Composed output per install (this install):
    - dm CLAUDE.md:    `` `dm` role label ``    (was `` `DM` role label ``)
    - pm CLAUDE.md:    `` `pm` role label ``    (was `` `PM` role label ``)
    - qa CLAUDE.md:    `` `qa` role label ``    (was `` `QA` role label ``)
    - skill CLAUDE.md: `` `skill` role label `` (was `Your role label`)
    
    Composed-size deltas: zero (1 char per role on these single lines).
    
    Portability win: install verifier-aliased-to-`qe` would now show
    `` `qe` role label `` in BOTH the statusline AND the verifier doc.
    
    Closes: G10 (statusline label coupling).

